+    """WHICH PROOF a checkpoint's fence is, for a reader that must say.
+
+    W385695 R1. Two kinds exist and no reader may treat one as the other: the
+    writer's committed assignment fence (`ASSIGNMENT_FENCE_KIND`), and the
+    recovery fence (`RECOVERY_FENCE_KIND`) under which the line owner froze an
+    owner-approved recovered candidate for a writer that was never released.
+
+    THE ENVELOPE IS THE COLUMN'S OWN CONTRACT -- `intent` and `fenced`, which
+    `LINE_CHECKPOINT_COLUMNS` and `_fence` both hold every checkpoint fence to
+    -- and the KIND is what the intent says it is. An assignment intent is the
+    closed `attempt.finalize-intent` document, which has no `kind` member and
+    refuses one; a recovery intent is the closed document below, which names
+    its kind and is refused by the finalization reader. So neither can be
